---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'scope', title: 'Scope of this policy' },
  { id: 'information', title: 'Information you provide' },
  { id: 'sensitive', title: 'Sensitive information' },
  { id: 'technical', title: 'Hosting and technical data' },
  { id: 'use', title: 'How information may be used' },
  { id: 'sharing', title: 'When information may be shared' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'Security and retention' },
  { id: 'residences', title: 'Residence privacy' },
  { id: 'choices', title: 'Your choices' },
  { id: 'links', title: 'Other websites' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact us' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  intro="How information connected with this public website is handled, and what should never be submitted through a general inquiry form."
  description="Privacy information for visitors to the New Beginnings Transitional Living Foundation website."
  updated="August 21, 2026"
  sections={sections}
>
  <p class="legal-intro">
    New Beginnings Transitional Living Foundation respects the privacy of prospective
    residents, current residents, families, referral partners, donors, and other visitors.
    This policy explains the limited role of this public website and how information connected
    with it may be handled.
  </p>
  <p class="legal-entity">
    New Beginnings Transitional Living Foundation ("New Beginnings," "we," "us," or "our")
  </p>

  <section class="legal-section" id="scope">
    <h2 data-label="Section 01">Scope of this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy applies to newbeginningspgh.org and to information you choose to provide
      through a public website form or another contact method identified on the site. It does
      not describe every record New Beginnings may maintain in connection with housing,
      nonprofit operations, employment, volunteering, or a professional referral.
    </p>
    <p>
      New Beginnings provides recovery housing. It is not a clinical treatment provider, and
      the public website is not a patient portal, treatment-record system, secure intake
      system, or emergency communication service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="information">
    <h2 data-label="Section 02">Information you provide</h2>
    <p>The public inquiry form may ask for information such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your first and last name</li>
      <li>Your email address and telephone number</li>
      <li>Whether you are contacting us for yourself, a loved one, a client, or another reason</li>
      <li>A short message explaining how New Beginnings may be able to help</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You may also provide information when you telephone New Beginnings. Please share only
      what is reasonably necessary for a general availability, referral, donation, or
      partnership conversation. More detailed information, when appropriate, should be shared
      through the private process New Beginnings identifies for you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="sensitive">
    <h2 data-label="Section 03">Sensitive information</h2>
    <aside class="legal-callout" role="note">
      <p class="legal-callout-label">Please protect your information</p>
      <div class="legal-callout-body">
        <p>
          <strong>Do not submit sensitive information through a general website form.</strong>
          Begin with basic contact information and a general description of what you need.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
    <p>Do not place any of the following in a public inquiry:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Medical records, diagnoses, medication information, or treatment histories</li>
      <li>Detailed substance-use, mental-health, or clinical information</li>
      <li>Criminal-history records, court documents, or supervision records</li>
      <li>Social Security numbers, government identification numbers, or passwords</li>
      <li>Bank, credit-card, insurance, income, or other financial-account information</li>
      <li>The exact address of a New Beginnings residence or another resident's private information</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A website inquiry does not create a confidential clinical relationship. If more
      information is needed, New Beginnings will explain an appropriate next step.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="technical">
    <h2 data-label="Section 04">Hosting and technical data</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted through Cloudflare. Like other hosting and security providers,
      Cloudflare may process technical connection and security information when a visitor
      requests a page. That processing is governed in part by Cloudflare's own terms and
      privacy materials.
    </p>
    <p>
      Website technology can change. We do not make a broader promise here about a particular
      analytics product, cookie, or form-delivery service unless that practice has been
      confirmed and described in a current version of this policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="use">
    <h2 data-label="Section 05">How information may be used</h2>
    <p>Information you choose to provide may be used to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to a general question or return your call</li>
      <li>Discuss general housing fit, current availability, and the next step in an intake</li>
      <li>Communicate with a family member, referral partner, donor, or community organization</li>
      <li>Protect the website and organization from spam, misuse, or security threats</li>
      <li>Maintain records reasonably connected with nonprofit operations or legal obligations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Information collected later through a separate housing, referral, employment, or other
      operational process may be governed by additional notices and procedures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="sharing">
    <h2 data-label="Section 06">When information may be shared</h2>
    <p>
      Information may be available to people who need it to respond to an inquiry or operate
      the organization. It may also be processed by service providers that support the public
      website, such as the site's hosting and security provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      New Beginnings may disclose information when required by applicable law or a valid legal
      process, or when reasonably necessary to address fraud, misuse, security, or an immediate
      safety concern. This policy does not authorize visitors to submit confidential records
      through the public website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="security">
    <h2 data-label="Section 07">Security and retention</h2>
    <p>
      New Beginnings takes reasonable steps appropriate to the public nature of this website.
      No website, email, telephone system, or method of electronic transmission can be
      guaranteed completely secure. Limiting a website inquiry to basic contact information is
      an important part of protecting your privacy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Website inquiry information may be kept for as long as reasonably needed to respond,
      maintain appropriate organizational records, resolve a concern, or meet a legal
      obligation. Retention may vary according to the nature of the communication.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="residences">
    <h2 data-label="Section 08">Residence privacy</h2>
    <p>
      New Beginnings does not publish individual recovery-residence addresses or identifying
      exterior information on this website. Neighborhood-level information allows people to
      understand the general service area while respecting the privacy and safety of residents.
    </p>
    <p>
      Exact location information may be shared privately when appropriate during the intake or
      referral process. Visitors should not use this website to request, disclose, or circulate
      another person's residence information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="choices">
    <h2 data-label="Section 09">Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You may choose not to use a website form and may call New Beginnings instead. You may
      also contact us to ask a reasonable question about information you previously submitted,
      or to request a correction or deletion. A request may be limited when information must be
      retained for a legitimate operational or legal reason, and identity verification may be
      required before a request is completed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="links">
    <h2 data-label="Section 10">Other websites</h2>
    <p>
      This site may link to government agencies, licensing information, recovery resources,
      nonprofit records, social services, or other organizations. New Beginnings does not
      control the privacy or security practices of those websites. Review their policies before
      providing information to them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="changes">
    <h2 data-label="Section 11">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated as the website, organizational practices, or applicable
      requirements change. The review date at the top of the page identifies the current
      published version. Material website-practice changes should be reflected here before or
      when they take effect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section" id="contact">
    <h2 data-label="Section 12">Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      For a question about this website privacy policy, call New Beginnings. Do not include
      sensitive personal information in a general privacy inquiry.
    </p>
    <div class="legal-contact">
      <p><strong>New Beginnings Transitional Living Foundation</strong></p>
      <p>Phone: <a href="tel:+14126280403">412-628-0403</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
